// Gama-G v0.2 core: state and authority.
//
//   ggc run examples/core/ledger.gg
//   ggc graph examples/core/ledger.gg
//
// Bindings produced by operations are single-assignment; nothing reassigns
// them, because there is no assignment.  The only things that change are
// `state` resources, and they change only through a declared `transition` that
// says what authority it needs and what must hold afterwards.
//
// The graph has two phases.  Compute operations produce bindings and are
// ordered purely by data.  Transitions commit changes afterwards.  A compute
// operation may not depend on a transition -- that would make the derived order
// depend on an effect rather than on data, which is the one thing this language
// refuses to allow.

gama core 0.2

intent Ledger
    purpose    record one deposit against a balance
    authority  AuditWrite
    trail      ledger movement

source amount : I64 from 100

state balance : I64
    starts     0
    authority  AuditWrite

operation Seen
    uses     amount
    yields   seen : I64
    effect   pure
    computes amount

transition Deposit
    alters   balance
    uses     seen
    effect   storage
    needs    AuditWrite
    holds    balance >= 0
    computes balance + seen
    trail    deposit

outcome balance
